T16:26:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable, 4.5-dev3\n\n### System information\n\nCachyOS - KDE Plasma 6.3.4 - Wayland\n\n### Issue description\n\nScrolling in e.g. node list or script editor feels responsive but *really* fast. Compare this with the X11 backend, where scrolling is not smooth (jumpy in most cases, weirdly laggy and interpolated in the script editor) but happens at much more sensible speed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Get yourself a device capable of scrolling at small steps - touchpads are the most obvious case, but perhaps certain mice also could do\n2. Enable the Wayland backend in Godot\n3. Try scrolling in anything scrollable\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo project required - clicking on the \"other node\" button in an empty project to bring up node selection dialog that has scrolling is enough.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use